    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear offensive ceiling anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (81.94) and **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88). Both players benefit significantly from a prime matchup against Elmer Rodr\u00edguez, whose elevated 5.31 xERA makes him the ideal target for our power-speed anchors. **Kyle Tucker** is particularly well-positioned, as favorable winds and an advantageous platoon split drive his efficiency well into our \"Strong\" tier, while **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s placement in the heart of the order provides the volume needed to maximize his base projection. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Heliot Ramos** (61.25) also profile as high-end starts against Shane Baz, with dynamic platoon advantages pushing their scores comfortably past the 60.0 threshold.\n\nConversely, we are exercising caution with the bottom of our lineup. **Nasim Nunez** (47.12) and **Sam Antonacci** (48.78) represent marginal starts; while they occupy roster spots, their utility is hindered today by unfavorable platoon matchups\u2014specifically for **Sam Antonacci** against Freeland\u2014and lower-order lineup protection. The most difficult personnel decision was benching **Liam Hicks** (39.22). Despite a decent platoon look against Wheeler, the sub-3.00 xERA of the opposing starter created an \"Elite Arm\" penalty that forced **Liam Hicks** below our mandatory 40.0 floor. We continue to monitor the status of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Luis Robert Jr.**, as the latter remains sidelined on the IL, leaving our bench rotation to focus on high-floor utility players like **Coby Mayo** (58.85), who earns a start today primarily on the strength of the matchup against Rodr\u00edguez. \n\nManagerial note: With lineups pending for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Coby Mayo**, these scores remain subject to minor volatility. Please ensure rosters are locked once official lineups are posted to account for any late-scratch risks that could shift these projections.",
